the drop-off point at liverpool women's  hospital in northwest england it's just  before 11am there's an explosion then  the driver can be seen getting out and  several people rushed to help him  he was injured but has now been released  from hospital  by the time fire crews arrived the taxi  was in flames and the passenger was dead  inside the vehicle  liverpool's mayor has called the  driver's actions heroic saying they  avoided in her words an absolutely awful  disaster i can't comment on the on the  details or or exactly what type of uh  incident it was what type of crime it  may have been  but it does look as though the taxi  driver in question did behave uh with  incredible presence of mind and bravery  this has now been declared a terrorist  incident  counter-terrorism police have been  involved in the investigation since  sunday hours after the incident police  arrested three men all in their twenties  at the same property in liverpool a  fourth person's now been detained police  say they found significant items at one  address  it is not clear what the motivation for  this incident is  our inquiries indicate that an  improvised explosive device has been  manufactured and our assumption so far  is that it was built by the passenger in  the taxi  the reason why he then took it to the  women's hospital is unknown  as is the reason for its sudden  explosion  police say the passenger had asked to go  to the hospital but they're checking  whether there's any link with  remembrance day events nearby  nadim baba al-jazeera
 

